{"answer": "Otto was planned for Cloud Run in europe-north1 (issue #27), chosen so the service would sit in the same region as the Vertex model. That plan was never built. Otto was deployed to the shared GKE cluster `n8n-cluster` in europe-west1, which is where the api, web and MongoDB run, and the deployment spec records this divergence. Issue #27 was closed as superseded. The region choice also lost its premise. Measurements on 2026-10-16 showed europe-north1 serves only the Gemini 2.5 models (pro, flash, flash-lite), which retire on 2026-10-20, and no 3.x or 4 model. The current models are served from the `eu` multi-region, so the model runs on Vertex AI's `eu` multi-region instead. ADR-003 (PR #416) records this and supersedes the unwritten ADR-001. The sources don't give a separate reason for choosing the shared GKE cluster over Cloud Run.", "sources": ["adrs/ADR-003-hosting-and-data-residency.md", "pull-416 (re-cinq/Otto PR #416)", "issue-27", "specs/support-agent-prompt-and-model/spec.md", "specs/support-agent-deployment/spec.md", "commit 5e726ef72fbd1764fc086b0a3e0bb806a0ccbf45"]}
```

